shploingus clean room — new code beside the old tree (Constitution P7)
derive-from documents: docs/CLEAN-ROOM-PLAN-2026-10-11.md, docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md, docs/APPEARANCE.md

The clean room's 13 unified systems (docs/CLEAN-ROOM-PLAN-2026-10-11.md §2, extended by §16):

[U1] Presentation  (slice 1) — specified + one measured behaviour
     unifies:       OpenPBR-input derivation, Source 2 stylisation, the GPU pipeline, sky, shell painting
     witness:       crates/voxel-appearance, crates/voxel-client (+ 7 .wgsl)
     derived from:  docs/APPEARANCE.md §1, docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md §2 F13, the FMA bar, LEDGER C-39
     must not copy: any file under crates/voxel-appearance or crates/voxel-client
     interface:     shade(surface, normal, light, view) -> Rgb; band_count; Renderer seam

[U2] World model and its vocabulary  (slice 2) — in progress (world, shapes, chain; audit findings fixed; axis vocabulary owed)
     unifies:       coordinates, the 4x4x4 lattice and 256x level, matter, materials, shapes, chain, tickets
     witness:       crates/voxel-model
     derived from:  docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md §1-§5, docs/SHAPERS.md §2, docs/MODS-MATERIALS.md, the Axis/Laya rules
     must not copy: crates/voxel-model source; the two generated materials files
     interface:     Coord; Subvoxel; MaterialRegistry; RefusalSet; ShaperSet; Profile; Chain

[U3] World generation (the shapers)  (slice 3) — in progress (15-stage roster declared and validated; 13 stage bodies landed; one digest at 1/2/4/8 workers; 2 stages refuse by name by decision — caves, whose dissolution field is not declared, and earthworks, the record and not a generator; delta's avulsion state is owed inside a landed stage)
     unifies:       noise primitives and the fifteen shaper stages plus the cadence runtime
     witness:       crates/voxel-noise, crates/voxel-shapers
     derived from:  docs/SHAPERS.md, docs/MISSING-SYSTEMS.md, docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md §2 F4-F10
     must not copy: any .rs under crates/voxel-noise or crates/voxel-shapers
     interface:     Declared; Stage; ShaperSet; ProcessScheduler; TickDriver; field_at

[U4] Meshing, streaming and work  (slice 4) — in progress (field-derived mesh with greedy merge; level ladder 0..=2; four typed horizons; resident set keyed by world truth with exact invalidation; work ledger counted where the work happens; budget by name; one digest at 1/2/4/8 workers; the displaced 256x level, the multi-chunk stitch, a strided field request and a streamed residency policy are owed)
     unifies:       sparse voxel octree, greedy mesh, 256x refinement, four horizons, resident set, pool, budget
     witness:       crates/voxel-mesh, crates/voxel-stream, crates/voxel-work
     derived from:  docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md §4 SPEC-3/SPEC-5, LEDGER C-43, C-46
     must not copy: any .rs under those three crates
     interface:     Mesh; Octree; refine; WorldSource; Horizon; Resident; Pool; Budget; TickReceipt

[U5] Instrumentation, light and audio  (slice 5) — built (2026-10-12, §24): the one sensor concept with the wall and the overlay as its consumers, a min/max band per item, a weighing gate whose answer is a mass and nothing else, the virtual gauge wall in one controller; one band table and the closed-form solver (sky, beam, twilight, the Moon as a reflectance, two-droplet geometries) and the onset layer's own read for the audio seam — a quantity that cannot be weighed is refused by name. Owed and named: ozone, an azimuth, the per-cell frame format, and the audio voices themselves
     unifies:       the sensor concept, min/max bands, the weighing gate, the gauge wall, the light solver, audio
     witness:       crates/voxel-instrument, crates/voxel-light, crates/voxel-audio
     derived from:  docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md §3 S-03/S-12/S-13, FC-2.16, docs/light-solver.md, docs/lighting-sky-and-moon.md
     must not copy: any .rs under those three crates
     interface:     Sensor; Band; GaugeReading; GaugeWall; Crossing; Mass (and nothing else); Solver; Spectra; the audio seam (onset, gain)

[U6] The record and the API layer  (slice 6) — in progress (the gate: a closed eight-row table, the canonical request line, the answer and its claims, the checks, the effect, the receipt, and the parse/world refusal split with the world's refusals recorded through the chain's one writer; the stdio transport: one line in, one response record out, served by the binary's `serve` mode and driven as a separate process by the binary's own evidence and the tests; the content gate: a declared row consumed **in place by reference** — as `intake`'s own seam and as the table's `admit` row, which arrives over the wire by reference (`path + digest`, never bytes) and answers what the row became — judged on **seven** named axes, `admit`/`inspect` -> `Established` and never a bool, with an unchecked axis never a pass and a pin still not a claim a request line can carry; the last axis is **conformance against the world's own declarations** — a row may require stages of U3's `Declared` and materials of U2's `MaterialRegistry` (the table's two **optional** arguments, `requires_stages`/`requires_materials`, whose absence is the declaration *this row requires nothing*), refused `stage_undeclared` with the stage named and `unadmitted_material` in the registry's own words, with a requirement that is **owed** or names nothing reachable through the intake's seam but not yet spellable by a served line, and with neither ever counted as a pass; `save`/`load` arrived as the seventh and eighth rows of the table (2026-10-12, §28) by reference, so the table is closed at eight and U9's document form reads through this gate; and the **policy chokepoint** landed (2026-10-12, §29) — `policy.rs`'s one decision function, every served row consulting it at one call site, with deny by default made structural (a closed action vocabulary and an exhaustive matrix with no wildcard arm), grants refused construction without a granter or a scope, a refusal that quotes the list, and every denial **recorded** on the one chain; owed: the gate's remainder — the document record and its compression, the structural judge, the ballot, the recipe, the API document, the policy matrix's **remainder** (the self-describing protocol and the tool-surface narrowing over a mod-supplied tool list, neither of which has a caller in this build) — and the legacy-vocabulary bijection)
     unifies:       intake gate, document record, structural judge, ballot, census, policy, recipe, apidoc, bridge
     witness:       crates/voxel-package (+ crates/voxel-mcp as transport)
     derived from:  docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md §2 F1-F2, docs/UI-SPEC.md, docs/SHELL-PORT.md, docs/MODS-MATERIALS.md
     must not copy: any .rs under crates/voxel-package; also must not carry bytes
     interface:     intake::{Source, Claim, Row, Requirement, Requirements, Axis, Establishment, Finding, WorldDeclarations, Intake::over/admit/inspect -> Established, Intake::census}; Compendium::derive; StructuralJudge; Ballot; recipe; apidoc::render; the policy chokepoint: policy::{Action, Scope, Grant, Caller, PermissionClass, permission_of, decide, check_matrix} consulted by the gate at one call site; bridge::TOOLS + Tool::action + Receipt; reference::{gate, caller, serve_stdio}; transport::serve

[U7] The decision layer (axis, laya, von)  (slice 7) — built (2026-10-12, §25): the seven ladders — three declared from documents, four **owed by name** — with the two prohibitions and round 5's bare-token rule, the coverage table's total pin and its anti-fabrication guard; the closed three-word verdict, the typed question, the ballot whose floor is declared before the answer exists, the structural-judge seam and the four fail-closed rules, each refused by its own name; and the classifier — the record's own declared facts (twelve features over the format's words) with its claim's fourteen features beside them, calibrated over the sixteen labelled records at five life stages — answering a ballot with `Origin::Oracle` while its leave-one-out accuracy beats the majority class (0.5000 against 0.3125, margin +0.1875, with the claim-only reading 0.0000 printed beside it because that is the finding that moved the question to the head). Owed and named: the four ladders' token lists (U12's vocabulary), the score instrument's rungs, the `noul`/`score` calibration sets (a `noul` question is **refused by name** until its set exists), and a model-backed instrument (this build's `von` is structural, on CPU, with no dependency added)
     unifies:       the seven axes, the Laya questions, the ballot, the calibrated oracle, the von classifier
     witness:       crates/voxel-model/src/{axis,laya}.rs, crates/voxel-package/src/{oracle,ballot}.rs, crates/voxel-von
     derived from:  the Axis rules in LEDGER (rule 51-55, round-5 bare-token), the plan's Lane C join, patches/PATCH-023 (the ballot), patches/PATCH-039 (the five stages, and that the stage question is answerable from heads)
     must not copy: any .rs under those files
     interface:     AxisKind + Ladder + refuse_interchange/refuse_reduction/refuse_bare + COVERAGE/check_coverage; Question{Choice,Score,Noul}; Verdict{Belongs,NotBelongs,NoReading}; Ballot; Measurement (four accuracies and the majority class); StructuralJudge + Unreachable; laya::answer and the four fail-closed rules; von::Classifier (Declared/Feature, calibrate, classified, carriers) and von::claimed_vocabulary

[U8] The game binary and the shell UI  (slice 8) — built (2026-10-12, §27): the only window — a Mount-shaped pane tree driven by a declared Recipe (six declared windows, and the mount adds none it was not handed, so there is no second registry), the shell/HUD layer toggle over one window set, the one pointer-ownership decision read once and passed by value into both the drawing and the grab so the glyph and the grab cannot disagree, the four-bucket admitted constants table (16 rows; an unadmitted name is refused by name) and a visibly drawn 100 × 30 frame whose panes read the systems already built (the registry, the reference world, its materials, the stage roster, a derived chunk's geometry and the light table). The `shell` mode is the interactive demonstration. Owed and named: undock, the splitter-drag resize, the console's five graded levels, the toast's final form, and the gholtzap/lintapple **P8** gate, which U13 owns and this slice does not take
     unifies:       the only window, the mount window manager, the design system, input ownership, the frame loop
     witness:       crates/shploingus, crates/voxel-ui, crates/voxel-client/src/shell
     derived from:  docs/SHELL-PORT.md, docs/UI-SPEC.md, docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md §3, portal_simulator.py's structure
     must not copy: crates/shploingus, crates/voxel-ui, shell/
     interface:     shell::Mount over a declared shell::Recipe (split/close/focus/toggle_layer/read_pointer/layout), the shell::Content readers, the four-bucket shell::CONSTANTS table, and shell::frame → a drawn Canvas; plus the binary's `shell` mode

[U9] Saves and loads, and the world's own seed systems  (slice 9) — in progress (the written form of a world: the exact length-framed encoding and its trailer; five declared per-domain stream seeds carried and checked in both directions; the ruleset identity; the record carried in its own wire form and declared by head and length; six named refusals; a real file round trip and one generation digest at 1/2/4/8 workers; and the **document form** — a world written at and read back from a declared reference (`path + digest`) through **U6's content gate**, the one place that gate is a hard prerequisite, carried as the table's own `save`/`load` rows and as `Save::read_document`. Owed: a save of a resident set, compression, and a versioned migration path)
     unifies:       the save, the load, and the seed systems of a world
     witness:       crates/voxel-client's `World` (seed + tick + config), crates/voxel-shapers' `WorldSpec` with its per-stage seed derivation
     derived from:  docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md §1.3 and §2 F1, SPEC-3; LEDGER C-96.1 and H-7.20; docs/CIVILIAN-PORT.md (GeneratorIdentity); docs/GAIA.md §5c/§11
     must not copy: those .rs files; and no legacy save format is the contract
     interface:     Save::of / Save::parse / Save::load -> Loaded; SaveIdentity; StreamSeed; Ruleset; LoadReport; and the document form: Document::write / Save::read_document, which reads only through U6's `Intake::read`

[U10] The gameplay tree the mods references imply  (slice 10) — in progress (the tree: **one entry per reference** in `docs/MODS-MAP.md` §1–§5, in the record's own order, each carrying the record's own four-word disposition — the count this build derives is printed beside the record's own figures, un-averaged — and **one row per technology** under the double-cover rule: 43 rows, each U6's own row, whose document is read **in place** and admitted through the gate the way an `admit` row is, so a document that is absent refuses `source_absent` and one whose bytes have moved refuses `source_digest_mismatch`, a refused reference refuses `licence_refused` by the owner's own name, and an owed reference is named and never admitted. Owed, and printed as owed: the recipe document's row-kind key and version, the duplicate-row refusal's name, a verb that serves the whole tree, and the per-row family assignment)
     unifies:       the ordered set of playable systems the mods references imply, as one declared tree of rows
     witness:       docs/MODS-MAP.md (**106 references** — 10 §1 + 42 §2 + 19 §3 + 35 §4, one row per reference with its clean-repo destination; its source file's 91 URLs and this repo's copy's 97 are counted in the header), docs/MODS-MATERIALS.md
     derived from:  docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md ruling 3 and §3's S-01..S-24 slots; docs/MODS-MAP.md §1-§5; docs/SHAPERS.md
     must not copy: any mod's code; and nothing derived may be implemented from a refused reference
     interface:     gameplay::Tree::of_record/entries/rows/first/declared/declare + Disposition + Entry + Technology; a tree of declared rows: feature, source document (path + digest), licence verdict, the system that carries it, its own acceptance check

[U11] planet shploingus (the planet-scale world)  (slice 11) — absent (admitted by §16; waits on U4's octree, refine and streamed residency policy, and on a declared scale/extent ruling — the 20-level ladder's 16 777.216 km is short of an Earth-sized circumference)
     unifies:       the planet as one world: its scale contract, its addressing, and the residency policy that lets it exist without being resident
     witness:       nothing in crates/ implements a planet; the outside tree's F:\planet-shploingus\docs\ART-DIRECTION.md is reference, never authority
     derived from:  docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md §5 and SPEC-5; docs/SHAPERS.md §2 (tectonics: Kreischer & Bommes 2019); docs/PLAN-2026-10-08-cloud-cubes.md
     must not copy: the outside tree; any .rs claiming to implement a planet here
     interface:     a declared scale/extent contract; U4's Octree + refine + Resident's streamed policy

[U12] Civilian organisations for mobs and autonomous players  (slice 12) — absent (admitted by §16; the **policy chokepoint** — U6's permission matrix — landed 2026-10-12 (§29), and U7's decision layer is **built** (§25), so what stands in front of this row is now **one** thing: U2's owed civilian/government vocabulary (T016). The organisation's nouns *are* that vocabulary, and an organisation this build invented without it would be a vocabulary beside the world's own rather than inside it)
     unifies:       the organisations civilians, mobs and autonomous players belong to and act through: membership, authority, permitted verbs, and the record of what was done
     witness:       crates/voxel-model/src/civilian (BLD-0221, whose `pub mod civilian;` is absent from that crate's lib.rs), the government vocabulary in LEDGER, docs/GAIA.md for an autonomous population
     derived from:  the Axis/Laya rules quoted in LEDGER; docs/GAIA.md §2-§9; docs/CIVILIAN-PORT.md as a document; DESIGN-SPEC §2 F11 and F8
     must not copy: civilian/**, axis.rs, laya.rs source
     interface:     Organisation with declared membership and authority; an actor that asks the one tool table what it may do; every act a governed event on the one Chain

[U13] The shell completed, and the gholtzap/lintapple gate  (slice 13) — absent (admitted by §16; waits on U1's remainder, U6's admitted constants table, U8, and the P8 gate, which its own acceptance check closes)
     unifies:       the mission's more complete shell as an acceptance surface: U1's shade and sky, admitted constants, and its own conformance gate
     witness:       crates/shploingus, crates/voxel-ui, crates/voxel-client/src/shell
     derived from:  docs/SHELL-PORT.md (the four-bucket rule), docs/UI-SPEC.md, docs/DESIGN-SPEC.md §3, portal_simulator.py's structure, the linter's own published rules
     must not copy: crates/shploingus, crates/voxel-ui, shell/
     interface:     U8's Mount pane tree plus the gate: the shell's drawn values and tool surface checked by P8, with the result recorded

